data.content:
Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with native-sized integers. Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

The test confirmed it compiles and runs correctly. On this 64-bit system, `nint` is 8 bytes (pointer-sized). One small gotcha: `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context since the size isn't known at compile time — use `nint.Size` instead.
